{"id": "c42dabe1-2e05-42de-9d7f-ecba526e43a9", "timestamp": "2026-10-21T06:39:33.585631", "source": "user", "parent_id": "7775661a-b3ad-48d8-a786-3a9350ecb95f", "llm_message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"cache_prompt": false, "type": "text", "text": "{\"researcher_request\": \"This is a design-only task for studying QuaRot's end-to-end 4-bit quantization impact on LLaMa-2 prefill and decoding performance. For this initial inspection, please provide ONLY the following three items — do NOT produce the full experiment design yet. (1) Input/repository inspection: survey the available materials in /workspace (any QuaRot / LLaMa-2 related files, README, configs, benchmark scripts, prior notes in track.md, etc.) and summarize what is on hand and what is absent. Note that runtime is bubblewrap with network disabled, no preinstalled dependencies, and no GPU; experimental execution is not required. (2) Proposed approach: a concise outline of how you would structure the experiment design — research questions, independent/dependent variables (e.g., quantization scheme, precision, sequence length/prefill tokens vs. decode step), model variants (e.g., LLaMa-2 7B vs 13B), proposed controls (FP16 baseline, weight-only vs end-to-end RTN/Hadamard/online variants where relevant), metrics (throughput, latency per token, perplexity, downstream task quality, memory footprint), profiling strategy distinguishing prefill vs decode phases, and any cross-layer or KV-cache considerations. (3) Consequential assumptions and uncertainties: list the assumptions you would need to make about QuaRot's rotation mechanics, LLaMa-2 specifics, evaluation harness, hardware proxy, and anything else not directly evidenced by the inspected inputs — and call out which of those could materially change the design. Keep the inspection focused and evidence-grounded; flag anything inferred.\", \"required_handoff_stage\": \"plan\", \"approach_approved\": false, \"public_task\": {\"question\": \"How does QuaRot's end-to-end 4-bit quantization affect the prefill and decoding performance of LLaMa-2 models?\", \"context\": \"Design an experiment that answers the question. The researcher can clarify source-supported setup details by topic. Do not claim that an experiment was run.\", \"environment\": {\"runtime\": \"bubblewrap\", \"network\": \"disabled\", \"repository\": \"/workspace\", \"python\": \"python3\", \"software_environment\": \"system Python; project dependencies not preinstalled\", \"datasets\": [], \"gpu_enabled\": false, \"cpu_affinity_count\": 24, \"note\": \"Successful exploratory commands are not proof of a completed experiment.\"}, \"researcher_topics\": [], \"question_budget\": 6, \"actor_step_budget\": 60, \"continue_after_initial_plan\": false}}"}], "tool_calls": null, "tool_call_id": null, "name": null}, "llm_response_id": null, "activated_skills": [], "extended_content": [], "sender": null, "kind": "MessageEvent", "source_event_index": 1}
