\"I1 inferred paper-level: QuaRot end-to-end 4-bit equals W4 weights plus A4 activations plus K4 V4 KV cache with rotations around q k v o gate up down linears and residual streams and online KV-cache rotation per decode step; if the reference uses K4V4 equal FP16 as a sub-variant, that becomes the primary QuaRot W4A4 cell.\", \"I2 inferred model-level: LLaMa-2 7B uses MHA (32 KV heads) and 13B uses GQA (8 KV heads); per-token decode cost of the online K V rotation kernel and the closed-form KV-cache size depend on this; if the reference disagrees, K4V4 savings attribution must be re-scaled.\", \"I3 inferred harness-level: QuaRot published quality uses WikiText-103 perplexity plus a small 0-shot downstream suite; if the researcher's harness differs, absolute numbers will differ but Delta-vs-FP16 should track.\", \"I4 inferred measurement-level: decode latency is reported per-token, not per-batch, because batching hides memory-bandwidth effects that dominate 4-bit decode; prefill is reported amortized over L.\", \"I5 inferred scope: 7B and 13B are within practical CPU/RAM budget; 70B is included only if researcher's reference GPU permits (optional, not default).\"], \"uncertainties\": [\"U1: does the researcher's end-to-end 4-bit include KV-cache 4-bit (K4V4) or only weights/activations? Determines whether the cell matrix has 1 or 2 QuaRot W4A4 cells.\", \"U2: is the FP16 control rotated-FP16 or vanilla-FP16? Determines whether rotation overhead is part of QuaRot's cost or absorbed as a methodological requirement.\", \"U3: what GPU model VRAM and bandwidth is available in the researcher's reference measurement setup? Without a GPU, kernel-level prefill-vs-decode attribution can only be extrapolated, not measured.\", \"U4: which evaluation harness and which calibration and evaluation data are used? Comparability with published QuaRot perplexity and 0-shot tables depends on this.\", \"U5: which definition of performance is primary when multiple compete: wall-clock late